  "query_preview": "/FRIDAY THROUGH TUESDAY/...\nIssued at 233 AM CST Wed Nov 4 2026\n\nAn upper level shortwave tracks across north central North Dakota on \nFriday, with height rises following in its wake through the weekend. \nThis will support temperatures staying around seasonal on Friday, \nwith highs continuing to climb through the weekend. For Friday, \nmostly expecting highs in the mid 50s, though could still see some \ncooler highs across north central Nebraska, where greater cloud \ncover could limit highs to the upper 40s. By the weekend, expect \nhighs push into the upper 50s to lower 60s as subtle ridging builds \nacross the northern Plains. With the ridging in place, no \nprecipitation is expected this weekend. \n\nLooking ahead to early next week, an upper level low tracks across \nthe southern Plains, with upper level ridging tracking across the \nnorthern Plains. This will continue to support a dry pattern. In \nfact, ensemble guidance shows virtually no chances for precipitation \nthrough at least the middle of next week. Temperatures are also \nexpected to be slightly above normal with this ridging. Highs early \nnext week are expected to push into the lower to mid 60s, which is \naround 10 degrees normal than usual for this time of year. However, \nsome of the warmer guidance does suggest potential that we could see \nhighs pushing into the upper 60s, particularly on Monday and \nWednesday.",
